> API and interpretation

A disconnected call returns only the tree of the starting component, rather than
an all-component forest. Self-loops and stale heap entries can be observed but
never become accepted tree edges. The selected event count excludes
heap-internal comparisons, allocations and input validation. With parallel
edges, a heap bound in terms of log(E+1) is appropriate; the report does not
import a simple-graph O(E log V) statement without its assumptions. Finite
total-weight overflow is checked.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Shortest connection networks and some generalizations, Robert Prim|https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1538-7305.1957.tb01515.x]

